{
  "version": "1.0",
  "_doc": "Declarative manifest read by app/services/attribute_engine. One entry per attribute. Adding a new attribute is a config change here + a normalization block in attribute_normalization.json. No code changes required. The `recommendation` block declares how each attribute participates in customer recommendation services: persona_relevant + score_weight (validator-enforced to sum to 1.0 across persona_relevant attributes) + usage. The `signal_tags` array is opt-in (1:1 with intent-layer signals; today only `saturatable`). The `_weight_reason` field is FREE-TEXT documentation of why each weight was set; no behavioural impact. Recommended values: 'initial_manual_tuning_v1' (hand-picked at first ship), 'suggester_v1' (set by weight_suggester --apply), 'override_<context>' (deliberate human override of a suggester run, e.g. 'override_fashion_team_2026Q2'). Evolution of weights is logged at seed_data/weight_history.jsonl.",
  "attributes": {
    "product_type": {
      "_doc": "Identity attribute. Discovered + governed via the existing taxonomy_admin pipeline (product_type-clustering script + approval). Declared here so persona_extraction_service and customer_recommendation_service can read it as a manifest source of truth without hardcoding the attribute name.",
